![](/weird-guys.png "A picture of a woman holding some birds in her hand up for inspection. She is not impressed.")

This is a list of weird little guys in the free software movement and adjacent
spaces. Request additions, removals, or changes [via
email](mailto:drew@ddevault.org); patches welcome.

**Don't harass these people**! Don't engage with them at all.

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
>
> ## Alex Gleason
> ![](/gleason.png "Alex Gleason performing an interesting gesture")
>
> **Known for**: nostr stuff
>
> Alex is a prominent figure in the nostr community, and an antagonist on FOSS
> social media platforms generally. He developed the software used for Truth
> Social, Donald Trump's fediverse
> thing,[[source]](https://www.reuters.com/technology/head-engineering-trumps-truth-social-app-resigns-2023-07-17/)
> and was banned from the Mastodon instance he used back in 2023 for being
> openly transphobic.[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20230330163111/https://blog.alexgleason.me/gab-block/)[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20230331173749/https://blog.alexgleason.me/trans/)
>
> This photo of him on the right is prominently displayed on his personal
> website.

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
>
> ## [Andreas Kling]($heading.id("kling"))
> ![](/akling.jpg "Andreas Kling")
>
> **Known for**: SerenityOS, Ladybird
>
> Andreas is the founder of SerenityOS and the Ladybird web browser. He posted
> in support of Charlie Kirk after his assassination,[[source]](https://x.com/awesomekling/status/1966456391146606806),
> gets triggered by the phrase "punch nazis",[[source]](https://x.com/awesomekling/status/1967178708852097278),
> and the idea of using gender-neutral pronouns in documentation.[[source]](https://github.com/SerenityOS/serenity/pull/6814)
> Andreas boosted [David Heinemeir Hansson](#dhh)'s tweets on DEI and
> the white supremacist "white replacement" theory,[[source]](https://x.com/awesomekling/status/1874518295350837401)
> and expressed solidarity with David's persecution for his "banal, mainstream"
> positions, positions which include, for example, the forced expulsion of
> non-white people from the
> UK.[[source]](https://x.com/awesomekling/status/1969350008538370216)
>
> Ladybird and Andreas have received sponsorships from FUTO, Cloudflare, Shopify
> and 37signals (i.e. David Heinemier Hansson), Proton, Jetbrains, Sourcegraph,
> and others.[[source]](https://ladybird.org/#sponsors)

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
>
> ## [Brendan Eich]($heading.id("eich"))
> ![](/eich.jpg "Brendan Eich")
>
> **Known for**: Mozilla co-founder, Brave browser
>
> Brendan got a lot of flack several years ago, resigning as Mozilla CEO, after
> he donated a few thousand dollars to support California's Proposition 8, an
> initiative that would have banned same-sex marriage in California.[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20200425070742/https://blogs.wsj.com/digits/2014/03/28/three-mozilla-board-members-resign-over-choice-of-new-ceo/)
>
> After Mozilla, he moved on to co-found and lead as CEO the Brave Browser,
> which he used to push his own cryptocurrency micro-payments
> system.[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20200725110058/https://techcrunch.com/2017/06/01/brave-ico-35-million-30-seconds-brendan-eich/)
> He used Brave to support the hate website Kiwi Farms, which has been alleged
> to have instigated several suicides as a result of their harassment, working
> with their site admins to pose Brave as a safe and secure means for their
> members to access the site and conduct their harassment.[[source]](https://samambreen.wordpress.com/2019/08/16/an-open-letter-to-brendan-eich/)
> Kiwi Farms also took advantage of Brave's crypto scheme for funding, which was
> brought to Eich's attention and never corrected.[[source]](https://www.change.org/p/brendan-eich-brave-software-stop-providing-a-revenue-stream-for-white-supremacist-paedophiles)

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
>
> ## [Bryan Lunduke]($heading.id("lunduke"))
> ![](/lunduke.jpg "Bryan Lunduke")
>
> **Known for**: The Lunduke Journal, "Linux Sucks"
>
> Bryan is a prolific YouTube personality, maintains a personal blog, and
> frequently tweets on his X account, using all of these platforms to push
> "anti-woke" ideas and conspiracy theories, and harass anyone he views as too
> progressive, trans, female, or black. Big fan of RedHat DEI conspiracy
> theories.
>
> Has a huge problem with transgender people and goes out of his way to harass
> them, misgender them, deadname them, the works.

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
>
> ## Daniel J. Bernstein
> ![](/bernstein.jpg "Daniel J. Bernstein")
>
> **Known for**: Popular cryptographic algorithms, e.g. Salsa20, ed25519
>
> Daniel is an well-known and influential cryptographer and former visiting
> professor at TU/Eindhoven,[[source]](https://www.researchgate.net/scientific-contributions/Daniel-J-Bernstein-69944562)
> where he has worked with his wife, Tanja Lange, the chair of the coding theory
> and cryptology group there.[[source]](https://cc.win.tue.nl/staff.html)
>
> Daniel and Tanja are associates of [Jacob Appelbaum](#jacob-appelbaum)
> and served as his PhD advisors.[[source]](https://research.tue.nl/en/persons/jacob-r-appelbaum/supervised-student-theses/)[[source]](https://www.hyperelliptic.org/tanja/students.html)
> One of the students under Bernstein and Lange at TU/e, Henry de Valence,
> resigned from their PhD program in 2016 citing patterns of harassment, abuse,
> and bullying at the hands of Jacob, Daniel, and Tanja.[[source]](https://medium.com/@hdevalence/when-hell-kept-on-payroll-somewhere-is-where-you-are-f419d3022d0)

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
>
> ## [David Heinemeier Hansson]($heading.id("dhh"))
> ![](/d-hansson.jpg "David Heinemeier Hansson")
>
> **Known for**: Ruby on Rails, Omarchy (founder); 37signals (CTO); Shopify
> (Board member)
>
> David, aka "DHH", is a multi-millionare who funds and boosts the "dark
> enlightenment" in FOSS. His Linux distribution, Omarchy, is a loose collection
> of vibe-coded scripts on top Arch Linux and a vehicle for soliciting
> investments from large companies (e.g. Cloudflare, Framework, Dell, Block,
> Dropbox)[[source]](https://omarchy.org/news/2026/08/omacom-foundation-launches-with-8-million/)
> to finance the projects of his weird little friends.
>
> He wrote a blog post, "As I remember London",[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20260401205851/https://world.hey.com/dhh/as-i-remember-london-e7d38e64)
> in which he uses numerous racist, fascist, and ethno-nationalist dog-whistles
> while calling for the ethnic cleansing via forced removal of non-white people
> from the UK and other countries.
>
> The Ruby on Rails leadership stood by David in spite of numerous calls for his
> removal from positions of power by members of the
> community.[[source]](https://davidcel.is/articles/the-dhh-problem)[[source]](https://tekin.co.uk/2025/09/the-ruby-community-has-a-dhh-problem)

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
>
> ## [Eric S. Raymond]($heading.id("esr"))
> ![](/esr.jpg "Eric S. Raymond")
>
> **Known for**: Open Source Initiative (disgraced co-founder); "The Cathedral
> and the Bazaar" 
>
> Eric is a creepy weird guy who writes racist, homophobic, and misogynist
> screeds everywhere he can. His uses his blog, "Armed and Dangerous; Sex,
> software, politics, and firearms. Life's simple pleasures…", to advocate for
> weird right-wing politics, such as strident support for Kyle
> Rittenhouse[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20260313003028/http://esr.ibiblio.org/?p=8752)
> and threatening to shoot
> communists[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20260411015133/http://esr.ibiblio.org/?p=8685).
> He said gay men deserved to get AIDS because of "unfettered
> promiscuity",[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20061207053952/http://esr.ibiblio.org/?p=26)
> quotes racist talking points about police
> violence,[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20190217144805/http://esr.ibiblio.org/?p=7239)
> and says organizations that try to get women more involved in FOSS are trying
> to entrap men with rape
> accusations.[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20170804102904/http://esr.ibiblio.org/?p=6907)
>
> Eric got kicked out of the OSI mailing lists for being a huge asshole back in
> 2020.[[source]](https://lists.opensource.org/pipermail/license-discuss_lists.opensource.org/2020-February/021328.html)

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
>
> ## Enrico Weigelt
> ![](/metux.jpg "Enrico Weigelt's avatar")
>
> **Known for**: Xlibre (founder)
>
> Enrico, aka "metux", is the founder of the Xlibre project, a fork of Xorg.
> Took the Wayland/RedHat DEI conspiracy theory to its natural conclusion by
> making an unwoke fork of the deprecated Xserver project to keep it alive. The
> code of conduct is just "404" in a text file, and the README has been cleaned
> up but was initially mostly just a rant about the RedHat DEI big-tech
> conspiracy theory.[[source]](https://github.com/X11Libre/xserver/commit/4839966900d948c5793064b5dccbdb3fd35f558b)
>
> The Xlibre community is radically inclusive, which is to say, a huge
> circlejerk of open Nazis and bigots with no moderation.

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
>
> ## Eron Wolf
> ![](/ewolf.jpg "Eron Wolf")
>
> **Known for**: FUTO
>
> Eron is the modestly wealthy founder of FUTO, an organization that funds
> software projects. He doesn't like the Open Source Definition[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20251022160356/https://futo.org/about/futo-statement-on-opensource/)
> and cites other weird little guys like [Bryan Lunduke](#lunduke) and [Eric S.
> Raymond](#esr) to make his case. Eron is friends with Curtis Yarvin, a notable
> techno-fascist and influence on JD Vance, and invited Curtis onto FUTO's
> platform for an interview in 2023.[[source]](https://peertube.futo.org/w/eSzKtjupL928QzxPXC5k2R)
>
> Associate of Louis Rossmann.

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
>
> ## [Jacob Appelbaum]($heading.id("jacob-appelbaum"))
> ![](/appelbaum.jpg "Jacob Appelbaum")
>
> **Known for**: Tor (former contributor), Freedom of the Press Foundation
> (former TAB member)
>
> Jacob is a cryptography and computer security researcher and disgraced
> ex-member of the Tor project. In 2016 ten people came forward to present
> serious accusations of sexual harassment, assault, and
> rape,[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20160910001406/http://jacobappelbaum.net/)
> ultimately leading this removal from the Tor project,[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20160623104201/http://www.itwire.com/business-it-news/open-source/73415-security-expert-appelbaum-no-longer-part-of-debian.html) Debian,[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20190820150807/https://www.nytimes.com/2016/07/28/technology/tor-project-jacob-appelbaum.html) and the
> hackerspace he co-founded, Noisebridge.[[source]](https://blog.noisebridge.net/post/145728465358/noisebridge-statement-on-jacob-appelbaum)
>
> He still works quietly and mostly out of the public view at
> TU/Eindhoven[[source]](https://cc.win.tue.nl/staff.html)
> and has been rumoured to pop up at events around Berlin in recent years. He is
> currently working on the Vula network encryption
> scheme,[[source]](https://codeberg.org/vula/highctidh/commits/branch/main) which is funded by
> NLnet.[[source]](https://nlnet.nl/project/Vula/)

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
>
> ## Michael B. Paulson
> ![](/primeagen.webp "Michael B. Paulson")
>
> **Known for**: ThePrimeagen Twitch/YouTube accounts
>
> Popular Twitch streamer and YouTube personality whose content isn't all that
> weird, but who is publicly associated with a bunch of weirdos this list. He's
> a speaker at Omacon 2026, [David Heinemeier Hansson](#dhh)'s conference for fashy
> weirdos,[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20260810191341/https://www.omacon.org/)
> and a donor to [Andreas Kling](#kling)'s
> Ladybird,[[source]](https://ladybird.org/#sponsors) and otherwise maintains
> associations with and financially supports people in a little network of
> weirdos.

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
>
> ## [Richard M. Stallman]($heading.id("rms"))
> ![](/rms.jpg "Richard M. Stallman")
>
> **Known for**: Free Software Foundation, GNU, GCC
>
> Founder of the Free Software Foundation and one of the most important figures
> in getting this whole thing off of the ground. Also the subject of credible
> rumors of harassing a lot of women over the years, and frequently writes on
> his website in defense of rapists, sexual harassment, sexual exploitation of
> minors, distribution of child sexual abuse material, and even bestiality and
> necrophilia. Stallman's behavior is extensively covered in The Stallman
> Report.[[source]](https://stallman-report.org/)

> []($block.attrs('weird-guy'))
>
> ## Vaxry
> ![](/vaxry.jpg "Vaxry")
>
> **Known for**: Hyprland
>
> Vaxry is the "edgy" founder and maintainer of the Hyprland Wayland compositor.
> He oversees a toxic community and participates in hate and bigotry,
> particularly towards LGBTQ+ folks.[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20250306212807/https://blog.vaxry.net/resource/articleFDO/RHMails.pdf) Downplayed an incident where moderators of
> his Discord server changed the pronouns of a trans person to deliberately
> misgender them, saying "on the Internet, let's be real, [he] is the
> default".[[source]](https://youtube.com/watch?v=nskemNa_Kn4)
>
> Got banned from Free Desktop after losing his shit when they privately warned
> him not to be a toxic jerk in their community spaces.[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20250306212807/https://blog.vaxry.net/resource/articleFDO/RHMails.pdf) Hates codes of conduct
> and inclusively in FOSS.[[source]](https://blog.vaxry.net/articles/2023-inclusiveActivists)
>
> Funded by Framework,[[source]](https://frame.work/nl/en/blog/framework-sponsorships) speaker at [David Heinemeir Hansson](#dhh)'s Omacon
> 2026.[[source]](https://web.archive.org/web/20260810191341/https://www.omacon.org/)

